author: pi-agent
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-5h6j,parent,"2026-08-28T15:22:32.702Z",claude,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T15:37:36.994Z",claude,"Measured, not claimed. The suite reaches 100 percent line, branch and function coverage across 36 files and 674 tests, and the docstring gate reports 177 documented declarations. The round-trip properties were then revert-checked, and the first attempt found a hole rather than confirming the tests: swapping the description and author lines in the canonical series encoding left all 27 series tests green. Every one of them compares a round-trip against itself, so they hold under any self-consistent encoding while a change to it would make every series object ever written unreadable. A series is a transfer format, so the encoding is now pinned to exact bytes by its own test, and that test is itself revert-checked: the same swap now turns it red while the other 27 stay green."
  "2026-08-28T20:11:17.753Z",pi-agent,"PR #48 evidence: the exact-byte canonical encoding test and fresh-store transfer and re-derivation tests passed inside the 675-test suite. npm run release:check passed with c8 at 100 percent statements branches functions and lines. This child remains closed with its revert-checked regression proof."
